WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.740
An ex-bowling prodigy with a rubber hand&nbsp;
and a now-faceless terrorist back from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.901
the dead... These iconic characters and more&nbsp;
are on their way back to a screen near you.

00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:13.920
It's time for a new generation of kids to worry&nbsp;
about shooting their eyes out. Several decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.000
after the classic holiday film A Christmas&nbsp;
Story was first released, a sequel is in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.320
the works. A Christmas Story Christmas will&nbsp;
bring back Peter Billingsley as Ralphie, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.580
elementary school-aged protagonist of the first&nbsp;
film, now all grown up and facing the holidays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.960
yet again. Also returning for the sequel are&nbsp;
Ian Petrella as Ralphie's brother, Randy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.760
along with Zack Ward, Scott Schwartz, and R.D.&nbsp;
Robb as Ralphie's trio of friends from school.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.540
The story follows Ralphie's return to&nbsp;
his childhood home in an attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.680
give his children a Christmas like the ones he&nbsp;
experienced as a kid. According to Deadline,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.120
"Ralphie reconnects with childhood friends,&nbsp;
reconciles the passing of his Old Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.120
and sows the seeds for the origins&nbsp;
of the beloved holiday classic."

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.480
A Christmas Story Christmas&nbsp;
hits HBO Max on November 17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.500
2022 and is directed by Clay&nbsp;
Kaytis and written by Nick Schenk.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:04.080
In 2020, Disney confirmed that a fifth installment&nbsp;
in the iconic Indiana Jones franchise is on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.780
way, once again starring Indy himself, Harrison&nbsp;
Ford. At 78 years old, Ford will likely retire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.100
his trademark whip and fedora by the end of&nbsp;
Indiana Jones 5, although the studio hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.463
indicated whether he'll pass the baton to a&nbsp;
younger generation or close out the franchise.

00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:25.363
"You show up every day. You do your&nbsp;
job. And then they just let you go."

00:01:25.363 --> 00:01:29.340
We do know he'll be joined in his adventure&nbsp;
by Phoebe Waller-Bridge of Fleabag fame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.820
playing Indy's goddaughter, Helena.&nbsp;
Mads Mikkelsen from Hannibal will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.240
play the villain. He'll be joined&nbsp;
by Oscar nominee Antonio Banderas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.320
and John Rhys-Davies will again play&nbsp;
Indy's trusted companion Sallah.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.020
In the director's chair for Indiana Jones 5 is&nbsp;
James Mangold. Mangold directed 2017's Logan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.520
which served as the sendoff for Hugh Jackman's&nbsp;
Wolverine and Patrick Stewart's Charles Xavier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.180
Logan offered a thrilling and satisfying&nbsp;
ending for Jackman and Stewart's characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:59.340
and earned Mangold an Academy Award nomination&nbsp;
for Best Adapted Screenplay. While Indiana Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.660
5 isn't likely to skew as dark as Logan, we&nbsp;
hope the farewell to our favorite archaeology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.468
professor will be just as moving when&nbsp;
the film hits theaters on June 30, 2023.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.620
In the age of sequels, remakes, and reboots of&nbsp;
what feels like every significant film ever made,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.460
revisiting one of cinema's most iconic&nbsp;
horror movies was inevitable. Sure enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.180
The Exorcist 2, 3 and 4 are in the&nbsp;
works from fright factory Blumhouse.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:26.160
The original Exorcist centers on a 12-year-old&nbsp;
girl, played by Linda Blair, who's possessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.660
by a terrifying demon. Her mother, played by&nbsp;
Ellen Burstyn, hires a pair of priests, played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.700
by Jason Miller and Max von Sydow, to perform&nbsp;
an exorcism. Spoiler alert: both priests died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.560
in the original film, and Miller and von Sydow&nbsp;
have since passed on, as well. But Burstyn will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.120
be returning to assist new protagonist Leslie Odom&nbsp;
Jr. as he seeks help for his own possessed child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.800
The first film in the new Exorcist trilogy&nbsp;
will be released in theaters on October 13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.480
2023, although there's a possibility the&nbsp;
following two films could premiere on Peacock.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.660
As far as bizarre action movie premises go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.560
it doesn't get much weirder than&nbsp;
Face/Off. In this bizarre blockbuster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.580
Nicolas Cage and John Travolta star as a&nbsp;
terrorist and an FBI agent, respectively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.900
who literally swap faces via a gnarly surgery&nbsp;
in order to each take each other's place.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.220
Even though – spoiler alert – Cage's&nbsp;
villainous Castor Troy is killed at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.180
end of the first film, a direct sequel is now&nbsp;
in the works from filmmakers Adam Wingard and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.080
Simon Barrett. Barrett and Wingard were quick&nbsp;
to clarify on social media that they have no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.160
intention of reimagining the original, which&nbsp;
Wingard considers "a perfect action movie."

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.020
Speaking to the Associated Press,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:32.400
Cage expressed enthusiasm at the possibility&nbsp;
of reprising his role in the sequel, saying,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.460
"I would love to get back into that&nbsp;
character and to work with Travolta."

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.440
"God, I miss that face."

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.600
Wingard has expressed interest in seeing&nbsp;
Cage return, telling Empire Online,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.600
"He's just having such a moment.&nbsp;
[...] A couple of years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.780
the studio maybe would have wanted&nbsp;
a hot, young, up-and-coming actor or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.260
something. Now, Nicolas Cage is one of&nbsp;
the hottest actors in Hollywood again."

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:59.520
Of course, as Cage's character is dead, so&nbsp;
it'll be interesting to see how they bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.240
him back. But in a world as crazy&nbsp;
as Face/Off, anything is possible.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.800
On his 35th birthday, Julius Benedict,&nbsp;
played by Arnold Schwarzenegger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.640
discovered he was separated at birth from his&nbsp;
twin brother, Vincent, played by Danny DeVito,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.140
after they were conceived in a lab as part&nbsp;
of a genetic experiment. Twins followed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:19.380
unlikely duo as they reconnected and&nbsp;
uncovered the secrets of their past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.820
Thirty-three years later, the Benedict&nbsp;
clan is expanding once again in Triplets.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.480
This time Schwarzenegger and DeVito&nbsp;
will be joined by Tracy Morgan as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.200
a yet-unnamed third brother. Twins&nbsp;
director Ivan Reitman was slated to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.940
direct the sequel until his death in 2022. In&nbsp;
describing the sequel, Reitman told Deadline,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.780
"They don't know each other, and very early&nbsp;
in the movie, they meet. It's how they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.140
achieve a bond together after all these&nbsp;
years. It's really a film about family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.960
and no matter how different we all&nbsp;
are, we have to learn to get along."

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.560
Originally, the film was set to&nbsp;
begin shooting in 2022 from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.400
script penned by Dylan Dawson and Lucas&nbsp;
Kavner. Without Reitman at the helm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.560
we wouldn't be surprised if&nbsp;
production gets pushed back.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.540
It was just a matter of time before the&nbsp;
bizarre 1988 Tim Burton haunted house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:04.980
comedy Beetlejuice got the sequel treatment.&nbsp;
Sure enough, Beetlejuice 2 is finally in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.760
works from Brad Pitt's production company&nbsp;
Plan B, with Michael Keaton and Winona&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.780
Ryder expected to reprise their roles from&nbsp;
the first film. Beetlejuice starred Keaton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.263 --> 00:05:22.503
"If you don't let me gut out&nbsp;
this house and make it my own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.503 --> 00:05:24.700
I will go insane and I will take you with me!"

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.500
However, nothing goes according to plan. Lydia&nbsp;
Deetz, the new homeowners' quirky teenage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:34.000
daughter, played by Ryder, only narrowly escapes&nbsp;
being married off to him. By the end of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.200
the Deetzes and the Maitlands are happily&nbsp;
cohabitating, with Beetlejuice banished to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.460
a waiting room for the non-living. Although the&nbsp;
script for Beetlejuice 2 hasn't yet been written,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.480
we imagine it will find him finally&nbsp;
returning to find Lydia all grown up. How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.001
his path will cross that of his reluctant&nbsp;
ex-fiancée is currently anyone's guess.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:56.260
Directed by the one and only John Carpenter,&nbsp;
the 1986 fantasy-adventure Big Trouble in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.220
Little China follows trucker Jack Burton,&nbsp;
played by Kurt Russell, as he's drawn into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:04.480
the mystical underbelly of San Francisco's&nbsp;
Chinatown. Hoping to save a kidnapped woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.740
from the forces of darkness, Burton encounters&nbsp;
ninjas, monsters, and an ancient sorcerer.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:11.620
With its mythic warriors and magical sword fights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.100
Big Trouble in Little China has become&nbsp;
a classic, so, naturally, people were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.960
concerned when a remake with Dwayne Johnson was&nbsp;
announced in 2015. As it turns out, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:24.700
the next film will actually be a sequel. Speaking&nbsp;
to Collider, producer Hiram Garcia admitted,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:28.060
"You can't remake a classic like [Big&nbsp;
Trouble], so what we're planning to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.780
is continue the story. We're going to continue&nbsp;
the universe of Big Trouble in Little China."

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.800
Garcia went on to explain that the events&nbsp;
of the first film will still exist in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.920
new Dwayne Johnson movie, but the Rock&nbsp;
will be playing a brand new character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.820
While that leaves room for Russell's return,&nbsp;
the actor has said that he "probably won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:46.660
be" in the sequel. Fans will definitely&nbsp;
miss seeing Jack Burton back in action.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.000
We thought the day would never come, but it looks&nbsp;
like Ridley Scott is heading back to ancient Rome.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.380
"At my signal, unleash hell."

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.820
Nearly 20 years after the original&nbsp;
Gladiator hit theaters, Scott is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:05.020
finally making a sequel to the story&nbsp;
of Maximus Decimus Meridius. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.220
Maximus is busy walking through wheat fields in&nbsp;
heaven, so what's the sequel going to be about?

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:14.320
According to producer Walter F. Parkes, the&nbsp;
film starts 25 to 30 years after the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.340
ended. And according to The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, part two will focus on Lucius,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:23.680
the son of Maximus' old flame, Lucilla. It does&nbsp;
sound like Connie Nielsen, who played Lucilla,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.460
could come back. Speaking to Collider, Nielsen&nbsp;
said that the sequel was still planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.160
and when asked if she'd be willing&nbsp;
to return to the role, she said,

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.000
"It would obviously be amazing, and I know&nbsp;
that a lot of people want to see more of that."

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.960
Scott revealed in late 2021 that&nbsp;
the script is already complete,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.800
and Gladiator 2 is queued up to be the&nbsp;
director's next project once he's finished&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.520
with Napoleon. With Scott at the helm,&nbsp;
we're pretty sure we'll be entertained.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.040
Fans of the 1996 bowling comedy Kingpin are&nbsp;
in luck because a sequel is rolling down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.420
the pipeline. The original film featured Woody&nbsp;
Harrelson as a former bowling prodigy who believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:59.680
he's found his meal ticket when he discovers an&nbsp;
Amish bowling superstar, played by Randy Quaid.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:00.974
"Fourteen karat gold."

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:03.667
"Really? Looks like rubber."

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.340
"No. The ring, not the hand."

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.580
The film also starred Bill Murray&nbsp;
as Harrelson's lifelong rival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.460
as well as Vanessa Angel,&nbsp;
Chris Elliott, and Lin Shaye.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:17.200
No details have yet been revealed about the&nbsp;
sequel other than that Peter and Bobby Farrelly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:22.240
who directed the first film, will be back on&nbsp;
board to produce Kingpin 2. However, it's unclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.200
whether the Farrelly brothers are intending to&nbsp;
write or direct the sequel in addition to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:31.180
producing duties. Similarly, none of the original&nbsp;
cast is confirmed to be returning, although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.780
fans would surely welcome another chance to see&nbsp;
Harrelson and Murray together on the big screen.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.340
Jim Henson's cult classic Labyrinth&nbsp;
has a diehard following thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:43.360
its creepily fantastical storytelling,&nbsp;
imaginative creature creations, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.101
of course, an iconic performance from&nbsp;
David Bowie as Jareth the Goblin King.

00:08:47.101 --> 00:08:49.681
"I wish the goblins would come and take you away."

00:08:49.681 --> 00:08:53.320
Making a sequel to Henson's final feature&nbsp;
film is a pretty intimidating task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.300
but the Jim Henson Company feels up to it.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.240
News of the Labyrinth sequel first broke in 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:03.340
with Don't Breathe filmmaker Fede Alvarez&nbsp;
attached to direct. However, Alvarez announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:07.480
in April of 2020 that he was stepping away&nbsp;
from the film. He told Bloody Disgusting,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:11.440
"I just decided I didn't want to do things&nbsp;
as a director that people knew already what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.760
it was. Or have a preconceived notion of how it&nbsp;
should look on the screen. So Labyrinth would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:18.640
be something that people would judge&nbsp;
that way, so I decided not to do it."

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.860
Fortunately, the project didn't stay rudderless&nbsp;
for long. In May of 2020, Deadline reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:27.940
that Doctor Strange director Scott Derrickson had&nbsp;
stepped in to helm the highly anticipated sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:32.560
Maggie Levin, the writer and director of Into&nbsp;
the Dark, will write the screenplay. We don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.940
have any details about the plot, but back when&nbsp;
Alvarez was attached, project insiders confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:40.960
to The Hollywood Reporter that the sequel would&nbsp;
be a continuation of the story that began in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.002
original film. As Bowie has passed on, however,&nbsp;
the Goblin King will not be making an appearance.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.180
The first Lethal Weapon hit theaters in 1987,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:53.800
introducing audiences to the buddy cop duo&nbsp;
of Riggs, played by Mel Gibson, and Murtaugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:58.420
played by Danny Glover. Since then, it's spawned&nbsp;
three sequels and a television series. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:02.740
with no new Lethal Weapon films since&nbsp;
Lethal Weapon 4 in 1998, it was a surprise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.220
to learn that Warner Brothers intended to&nbsp;
reinvigorate the franchise with a new entry.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:09.700
Prior to the death of acclaimed director&nbsp;
Richard Donner — who directed the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.540
four Lethal Weapon films in addition to&nbsp;
Superman and The Goonies — producer Dan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:16.360
Lin said that the fifth film was&nbsp;
particularly special to Donner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.020
who was attached to direct. In 2020,&nbsp;
Lin told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:23.320
"We're trying to make the last Lethal&nbsp;
Weapon' movie. Donner's coming back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.040
The original cast is coming back. And&nbsp;
it's just amazing. The story itself is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.460
very personal to him and to the cast,&nbsp;
and so I really want to make that one."

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:35.380
Of course, none of that may pan out,&nbsp;
as Donner passed away in 2021. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.260
in the wake of the filmmaker's death,&nbsp;
Mel Gibson has confirmed that he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:42.421
in talks to take over directorial duties,&nbsp;
although a deal has not yet been reached.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:47.560
It's been almost 20 years since audiences&nbsp;
followed effervescent sorority girl Elle Woods to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:52.060
Harvard Law School in the bubblegum-hued Legally&nbsp;
Blonde. She continued to ascend the professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:56.980
ladder in 2003's Legally Blonde 2: Red, White &amp;&nbsp;
Blonde, which saw Elle head to Washington, D.C.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:00.967
"Hello, Patriots!"

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:05.440
Now Elle is back, along with producer Marc&nbsp;
Platt and Platt Productions president Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.460
Siegel. In addition to playing Elle, Reese&nbsp;
Witherspoon is producing through her Hello&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:14.020
Sunshine banner. She's brought on Never Have I&nbsp;
Ever creator Mindy Kaling and Brooklyn Nine-Nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:18.340
creator Dan Goor to pen the screenplay. Also&nbsp;
returning for the sequel is Jennifer Coolidge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:21.247
who starred in both previous&nbsp;
films as Elle's friend Paulette.

00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:27.834
"I love snow globes. I can hear the ocean!"

00:11:27.834 --> 00:11:30.400
There will be "a lot of new&nbsp;
faces" in Legally Blonde 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:32.980
and a lot more diversity. Kaling told E! Online,

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.240
"Reflecting the world as it is now is something&nbsp;
that's really important to Reese, and so having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.020
there be like diversity is super, super&nbsp;
important. You can definitely count on that."

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.700
A fan of the original film, Kaling is looking&nbsp;
forward to revisiting an older and wiser – and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:50.080
likely even more fabulous – Elle Woods. In&nbsp;
an interview with Access Hollywood, she said,

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:53.500
"I can't wait to see what Elle Woods — what&nbsp;
people will think of the way we wrote Elle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.600
Woods at 40. How Elle Woods is at 40 versus how&nbsp;
she was at 21 has been really fun to imagine."

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:03.400
But for those who worry that Elle may have&nbsp;
outgrown the Bend and Snap, Kaling reassured fans,

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:07.600
"Bend and Snap is forever. We definitely have a&nbsp;
lot of fan favorites from the original movie."

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:13.060
Despite nearly four decades having passed since&nbsp;
The Last Starfighter first wowed audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:17.620
the time may be ideal for a sequel. Starfighter&nbsp;
is about a teenager who beats a video game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.680
only to discover that the game is&nbsp;
really a recruiting tool looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.492
for soldiers to fight an interstellar alien war.

00:12:23.492 --> 00:12:26.312
"I've seen 'em come and I've&nbsp;
seen 'em go, but you're the best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:31.240
my boy. Dazzling. Light years ahead of the&nbsp;
competition. Which is why Centauri is here."

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:35.560
Video games have changed a lot since then, which&nbsp;
presents an interesting way to continue the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:40.120
story. Speaking to Moviehole, Jonathan Betuel, the&nbsp;
writer of the original film, said of the sequel,

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.800
"It's not a remake. It's going to continue the&nbsp;
story. What's changed is time itself, certainly as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.420
the video world and the alien world have continued&nbsp;
to tick away. It's not a time capsule of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:54.040
'80s by any means, we're taking it to the next&nbsp;
level. Passing the torch ... or the joystick."

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.120
Betuel will be co-writing the sequel, titled&nbsp;
The Last Starfighters, with Rogue One:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:01.840
A Star Wars Story screenwriter&nbsp;
Gary Whitta. In March 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:06.100
Whitta tweeted a sizzle reel that teases the&nbsp;
plot of the film. From what we can gather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:10.420
the story involves an alien attempting to&nbsp;
assassinate an adult Alex, the protagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:14.380
of the first film. Alex then heads off into&nbsp;
space to get to the bottom of things. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:18.222
been a long road, but Betuel is optimistic&nbsp;
the sequel will finally get off the ground.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:23.020
The last National Treasure film hit&nbsp;
theaters back in 2007. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:26.382
it's been a long time since we've&nbsp;
seen Benjamin Franklin Gates.

00:13:26.483 --> 00:13:27.983
"The treasure is a myth."

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.312
"I refuse to believe that."

00:13:31.312 --> 00:13:35.380
There have long been rumors of a third National&nbsp;
Treasure film, and while at times the project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:39.880
has seemed as lost as an ancient stash of gold,&nbsp;
it looks like a new installment is finally on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:45.400
the way. In May 2022, producer Jerry Bruckheimer&nbsp;
confirmed the film is in progress, with a script&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:50.140
by Bad Boys for Life scribe Chris Bremner. The&nbsp;
next step was to send the finished screenplay to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:54.280
original franchise star Nicolas Cage. The&nbsp;
project is apparently still in the works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.858
despite Disney moving forward with Disney+&nbsp;
series National Treasure: Edge of History.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:04.180
Along with Clerks 3, another Kevin Smith script&nbsp;
that got polished during the 2020 lockdown is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:09.220
the sequel to 1995's Mallrats, which he penned&nbsp;
under the working title Twilight of the Mallrats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:13.360
The plot of the original film revolves around a&nbsp;
dating show being filmed at a shopping mall, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:18.460
stars Jeremy London, Jason Lee, Claire Forlani,&nbsp;
Shannen Doherty, Ben Affleck, and Michael Rooker.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.020
This time, instead of a game show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:23.500
the plot will focus on a convention taking&nbsp;
place at the mall. According to Smith,

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.840
"The whole thing is, there's&nbsp;
a big convention at the mall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.840
so there's plenty of places and&nbsp;
opportunities [for things to happen]."

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:33.160
Smith has revealed that the entire principal&nbsp;
cast of the first film will be appearing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:37.660
the second. He even confirmed that iconic comic&nbsp;
book creator Stan Lee, who passed away in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:42.940
will have a scene to parallel his cameo in the&nbsp;
first movie. Smith confided to ComicBook.com,

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:47.620
"The thing I feel most clever about in regard to&nbsp;
the movie, obviously one of us can't come back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.120
right? Stan's gone. So, there is a Stan Lee&nbsp;
scene, and it makes absolute perfect sense.".

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.080
Joining the team for Twilight of the&nbsp;
Mallrats is newcomer Aparna Brielle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.500
whom Smith says will be at the&nbsp;
center of the sequel. He tweeted,

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:04.300
"I was so impressed with [Brielle], I built my&nbsp;
next flick around her. Aparna will play Brodie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.800
Bruce's daughter Banner in the movie I hope&nbsp;
to shoot next — TWILIGHT OF THE MALLRATS."

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.134
Twilight of the Mallrats is likely to&nbsp;
wind up as a Peacock exclusive release.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.380
It's been more than 30 years since we last saw&nbsp;
the fuzzy little nightmares who shouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:20.860
fed after midnight, but it sounds like the&nbsp;
Gremlins could be returning to theaters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:25.120
a new horrific adventure. A sequel to the&nbsp;
original movie, Gremlins 2: The New Batch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:29.500
was released in 1990. Original Gremlins&nbsp;
screenwriter Chris Columbus has apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:34.000
been working on getting a third Gremlins off&nbsp;
the ground. In November 2020, he told Collider,

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:38.200
"I would love to do it. I wrote a script [...]&nbsp;
We're working out some rights issues right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.260
so we're just trying to figure out when&nbsp;
the best time to make that film would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:45.820
be. I would still do it the same way -– I&nbsp;
would do it as tangible puppets, not CGI."

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:50.620
The "rights issues" involve Warner Brothers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:54.400
which now owns the name and franchise and&nbsp;
greenlit an animated Gremlins series for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.400 --> 00:16:00.220
HBO Max called Gremlins: Secrets of the Mogwai.&nbsp;
Still, Gremlins director Joe Dante told /Film,

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:04.720
"I think it's inevitable. The title is too well&nbsp;
known to not do something with. So eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:09.034
somebody's going to do something with it, which&nbsp;
is fine as long as there isn't too much CGI."

00:16:09.576 --> 00:16:15.220
RoboCop is back. According to Deadline, the cyborg&nbsp;
is returning to the big screen, although it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:19.960
the new film's going to mess with continuity. The&nbsp;
original RoboCop was directed by Paul Verhoeven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:24.940
and it made a killing when it was released&nbsp;
in 1987. After two sequels in the early '90s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:30.400
the franchise was rebooted in 2014 with actor&nbsp;
Joel Kinnaman and director Jose Padilha.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:34.960
The latest entry in the franchise will be called&nbsp;
RoboCop Returns, and will feature a fresh cast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:40.660
In November 2019, Orion Pictures announced that&nbsp;
Little Monsters director Abe Forsythe had taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:45.820
up the helm of RoboCop Returns. The screenplay&nbsp;
was originally written in 1998 by Ed Neumeier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:50.260
and Michael Miner, the scribes behind the first&nbsp;
film, with director Forsythe giving it a rewrite.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:54.340
Neumeier had nothing but good things to say&nbsp;
about the new version, telling Syfy Wire,

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:58.420
"What he came back with was really interesting,&nbsp;
it felt relevant and really crackled."

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:04.120
Dave Stevens' '80s cult comic book The Rocketeer&nbsp;
clearly took inspiration from mid-century movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:08.860
matinee adventure serials, and, in 1991, things&nbsp;
came full circle when Disney brought the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:14.140
to the big screen. Billy Campbell starred as&nbsp;
Cliff Secord, a 1930s stunt pilot living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:18.400
Los Angeles who finds a jetpack that allows him&nbsp;
to soar through the sky while evading the FBI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:23.140
its inventor Howard Hughes, and the Nazis who&nbsp;
want it badly. Disney thought it could launch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.920
a trilogy, but, when the film underperformed&nbsp;
at the box office, sequel plans were dead.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:31.720
In 2020, the company started work on a&nbsp;
legacy-style sequel to be titled The Return of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:36.760
Rocketeer. Now You See Me screenwriter Ed Ricourt&nbsp;
is writing the film, with actor David Oyelowo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:41.260
producing and possibly starring. The upcoming&nbsp;
Rocketeer movie will follow a new character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:45.880
a retired member of the famed Tuskegee Airmen who&nbsp;
becomes the latest pilot to strap on the fantastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:51.242
jetpack. While we don't know when it will be&nbsp;
released, we do know it will land on Disney+.

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:55.540
We are in the midst of an Eddie Murphy&nbsp;
renaissance. After his heyday in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:59.680
'80s and early '90s, Murphy faded from the&nbsp;
spotlight. He's suddenly back in a big way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:04.240
giving a critically acclaimed performance&nbsp;
in 2019's Dolemite Is My Name, making a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:08.680
triumphant return to Saturday Night Live as host,&nbsp;
lining up new standup comedy special for Netflix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:12.801
and announcing a sequel to one of his&nbsp;
biggest movie hits, Beverly Hills Cop.

00:18:12.801 --> 00:18:15.101
"Yes, you have a reservation for an Axel Foley."

00:18:15.101 --> 00:18:17.980
Marking the fourth installment in&nbsp;
the Beverly Hills Cop franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:22.420
the latest sequel will be a collaboration between&nbsp;
Murphy and Netflix, since Paramount pulled the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:28.300
plug on Beverly Hills Cop 4 back in 2016. Murphy&nbsp;
will be back as Axel Foley, the Detroit cop who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:32.860
repeatedly finds himself investigating crimes&nbsp;
in Beverly Hills. Directing will be Mark Molloy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:36.220
a rising filmmaker who's earned positive&nbsp;
attention for his Apple commercials.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:40.840
Murphy has said he's ready to go as soon as the&nbsp;
script is complete, and Will Beall, best known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:45.040
for story credits on Aquaman and Zack Snyder's&nbsp;
Justice League, has taken on Beverly Hills Cop:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:49.720
Axel Foley. Joining Murphy will be Zola breakout&nbsp;
star Taylour Paige and veteran actors Joseph&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:53.980
Gordon-Levitt and Kevin Bacon. Additionally,&nbsp;
Judge Reinhold tweeted some photos in September&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:58.480
2022 that hint he'll return as Foley's partner&nbsp;
in crime fighting, Detective Billy Rosewood.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:03.520
After writing and directing the classic&nbsp;
indie horror movies The Evil Dead and Evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:07.480
Dead II — but before he became the A-lister&nbsp;
behind the original Spider-Man trilogy — Sam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:11.380
Raimi ventured into the superhero realm for&nbsp;
the first time with Darkman. It's a dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:15.940
comic book-like revenge thriller about a scientist&nbsp;
who's presumed dead, but instead dons a hat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:19.900
trench coat, and thick facial bandages to take&nbsp;
revenge on the bad guys who nearly burned him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:24.100
to death. Oh, yeah, he's also super strong and&nbsp;
can create new faces out of experimental skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.280
but his disguises are sensitive&nbsp;
to light, so they never last long.

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:32.260
Darkman was one of the first big movies for&nbsp;
future superstar Liam Neeson and three-time Oscar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:36.520
winner Frances McDormand. A couple of obscure,&nbsp;
straight-to-video sequels to Darkman already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:42.220
exist. Raimi had nothing to do with those, and&nbsp;
he'd love to revisit the Darkman world. In 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:45.880
he told TheWrap that his sequel was in&nbsp;
the extremely early stages of development.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:50.434
"There's a producer attached. I haven't heard the&nbsp;
story yet or gone into it. But I think it's cool."

00:19:50.434 --> 00:19:54.760
Nothing in the way of creative crew, cast, or&nbsp;
release date has officially been confirmed.

